//? Title: Laplacian smoothing through actual Jacobi states
//? Subtitle: Original pinned noisy curve, energy descent and oversmoothing limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Smoothing graph-embedded vertices replaces local irregularity by movement toward
neighboring positions. That can reduce graph Dirichlet energy while also
shrinking geometry, oscillating at an extreme relaxation value, or increasing
error against a noiseless reference after too many passes. We inspect actual
synchronous centroid updates, retain the original41-point pinned curve
and40-pass result, and contrast energy descent with convergence and truth
preservation. Undirected reciprocal adjacency is checked before the energy
argument is used.
)

\toc

> The actual synchronous update

For each free nonisolated vertex, compute the neighbor mean from the complete
old state and write

$$ v_i^{new}=v_i+\lambda\left(\frac{1}{d_i}\sum_{j\in N(i)}v_j-v_i\right). $$
\alttext(A free vertex moves a fraction lambda from its old position toward the mean of its old-state neighbors.)

Pinned and isolated points stay fixed. All updates read the old state, so this
is Jacobi relaxation, not a sweep that immediately reuses an earlier vertex’s
new position. Duplicate neighbors count by multiplicity and self-loops
participate in the average. The complete graph must have reciprocal
multiplicities; otherwise the following undirected energy interpretation does
not apply. Missing suffix pin flags mean free vertices, preserving the
historical short-mask convention.

For one coordinate, let L be the symmetric graph Laplacian and D the diagonal
neighbor-count matrix on nonisolated free vertices. Undirected energy is E=x^T L
x, summing each edge once; pinned displacements are zero. The update
displacement is delta=−lambda*D^-1*g with g the free-coordinate energy-gradient
factor Lx. Since L<=2D as quadratic forms,

$$ E(x+\delta)-E(x)\le -2\lambda(1-\lambda)g^TD^{-1}g\le0,\qquad0\le\lambda\le1. $$
\alttext(The exact undirected energy change is at most minus two lambda times one minus lambda times a nonnegative weighted gradient norm.)

Apply this to both coordinates. This is an exact-arithmetic energy argument, not
an exact floating-point certificate or a mesh-untangling/shape-quality proof. At
lambda1 the bound need not be strict, and an unpinned bipartite graph can
alternate forever. A pinned graph can converge toward a harmonic embedding that
differs substantially from the desired underlying curve.

> One actual pinned-centroid update

Use points(0,0),(2,5),(4,0) on a path, pin both endpoints and set lambda1. The
only free point moves to the actual neighbor mean(2,0); exact energy falls
from58 to8. Every displayed value below is captured from that producing native
pass.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/laplacian_centroid.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/laplacian_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t =
        dm::geometry::laplacian_smooth_trace({{0, 0}, {2, 5}, {4, 0}},
                                             {{1}, {0, 2}, {1}}, {1, 0, 1}, 1, 1);
    std::print("| actual pass | original free vertex | neighbor reads | old x | old y | actual centroid x | " "actual centroid y | actual new x | actual new y |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.updates)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   e.iteration, e.vertex, e.neighbor_count, e.before.x,
                   e.before.y, e.centroid.x, e.centroid.y, e.after.x, e.after.y);
    std::print("\nActual original energy {}; actual final energy {}.\n",
               t.energies.front(), t.energies.back());
    const auto &e = t.updates.front();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("old", {0, 2},
           std::format("Actual old free vertex\n({}, {})", e.before.x,
                       e.before.y)).node("neighbors", {0, -2},
                                         std::format("Actual neighbor mean\n({}, {})",
                                                     e.centroid.x, e.centroid.y)).node("new", {7, 0}, std::format("Actual Jacobi output\n({}, {})", e.after.x, e.after.y)).edge("old", "new").edge("neighbors", "new").save_svg("build/laplacian_centroid.svg");
}
```
