> Oversmoothing the original reference

Perform one complete2000-pass trajectory on the original pinned curve and read
selected actual states. The harmonic path minimizing exact edge energy between
the fixed endpoints is a straight segment, with energy squared endpoint
displacement divided by40. That mathematical reference is not a promise of
closeness to the original sinusoid. The panels separate actual energy from mean
squared point error to that explicit noiseless curve. A log2(passes+1)
horizontal coordinate includes pass0 without a fabricated floor.

For each completed pass, a free nonisolated vertex reads its full neighborhood
once. Work counters count actual sweeps, updates, pinned/isolated skips and
neighbor-point reads; trace-only energy diagnostics are counted separately. Full
validation checks reciprocal multiplicities in O(E log(E+1)); subsequent I-pass
smoothing costs O(I*(n+E)) with two old/new state buffers. Capturing every
state/update and energy adds real memory and diagnostic work.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/laplacian_oversmoothing.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/laplacian_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <cmath>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto d = dm::geometry::laplacian_demo_curve();
    const auto t =
        dm::geometry::laplacian_smooth_trace(d.vertices, d.neighbors, d.fixed,
                                             .5, 2000);
    const double dx =
        d.vertices.back().x - d.vertices.front().x, dy =
        d.vertices.back().y - d.vertices.front().y;
    const double harmonic = (dx * dx + dy * dy) / (d.vertices.size() - 1);
    std::vector<double> x, e, error;
    std::print("| actual completed passes | actual state energy | actual mean squared point error | " "harmonic energy formula, exact-arithmetic reference |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i : {0, 1, 5, 10, 20, 40, 100, 500, 2000}) {
        const auto mse =
            dm::geometry::laplacian_point_mse(t.states[i], d.reference);
        std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} |\n", i, t.energies[i],
                   mse, harmonic);
        x.push_back(std::log2(double(i) + 1));
        e.push_back(t.energies[i]);
        error.push_back(mse);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), q = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, e, "actual", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, e, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4).line({x.front(), x.back()}, {harmonic, harmonic}, "harmonic formula", {22, 163, 74}, 2).y_limits(0, e.front() * 1.25).title("Actual Dirichlet energy and harmonic reference").x_label("log2(actual completed passes plus1)").y_label("squared edge-length energy");
    q.line(x, error, "actual MSE", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, error, "",
                                                            {220, 38, 38}, 4).title("Actual error to the original noiseless curve").x_label("log2(actual completed passes plus1)").y_label("mean squared point error");
    dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1).add(p).add(q).size(900, 850).title(
        "Energy descent can oversmooth the explicit reference").fit_panels().save_svg("build/laplacian_oversmoothing.svg");
}
```
