\caption(Actual energy descent and actual reference error on one complete native trajectory.)
\alttext(Both panels use the same stored states; the harmonic energy formula is explicitly theoretical, while the measured truth error can increase after oversmoothing.)

> Scope and verification

The complete input graph has finite points, exactly n adjacency rows and
reciprocal endpoint multiplicities, with n<=INT_MAX, pin-mask length at most n,
finite lambda in[0,1] and nonnegative iterations. Ordinary finite double
centroid/update order is preserved; widened parallel sums and convex-blend
fallbacks avoid some intermediate overflow, but produced finite-coordinate and
energy ranges remain checked. Trace energy uses long double; the historical
standalone energy API requires a finite double result. No face topology,
orientation, area or reference-truth invariant is inferred.

All states, updates and graph data are owned actual outputs. Complete capture
admission counts2*n+E+1 initial records plus iterations*(n+1+R) for R free
nonisolated updates per pass, before copies or smoothing. The million-entry
default excludes coordinate fields, capacities, final-result/runtime copies and
bytes/RAM; zero disables only that optional cap. No repeated-prefix smoothing
constructs the history.

Independent NumPy neighbor updates and energy sums verified100 graph studies
and600 actual states. Another500 complete ordinary smoothing paths matched
frozen trajectories exactly. Native tests exhaust64 four-vertex graphs,16 pin
masks and four relaxation values, and retain original pinned-curve, oscillation,
collapse, oversmoothing, reciprocal/loop/duplicate, finite-range and ownership
controls. The complete ten-report batch passed77 native CTest cases,39 directly
instrumented ASan/UBSan cases,106 compiled/executed public examples,479/479
scoped definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. All4 complete report
programs executed and all4 native figures were visually reviewed. HTML/Markdown
computed result and identical source/build/export figure bytes passed
verification. Repeatable receipts are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-194-203/`.

> References

G. Taubin(1995),
[A Signal Processing Approach to Fair Surface Design|https://doi.org/10.1145/218380.218473],
SIGGRAPH1995,351–358. This report uses a single-sign umbrella relaxation,
explicitly distinct from the paper’s shrinkage-reducing filter construction;
energy descent alone is not attributed shape-preservation or universal
truth-error guarantees.
